# Apache Flink DataStream API

## Overview
Apache Flink is a distributed stream processing framework for stateful computations over unbounded and bounded data streams. The DataStream API is the core API for processing streams of data.

## Key Concepts

### StreamExecutionEnvironment
The entry point for creating Flink streaming jobs:
```java
StreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();
```

### DataStream
Represents a stream of elements of the same type:
```java
DataStream<String> stream = env.addSource(new CustomSourceFunction());
```

### Sources
Sources are where data streams originate. Common sources include:
- `addSource()` - Custom source function
- `readTextFile()` - Read from text files
- Custom sources implementing `SourceFunction<T>` or `RichSourceFunction<T>`

### Transformations
Operations that transform one or more DataStreams into a new DataStream:

#### Map
Transform each element:
```java
DataStream<Integer> mapped = stream.map(x -> x * 2);
```

#### Filter
Filter elements based on a condition:
```java
DataStream<Integer> filtered = stream.filter(x -> x > 10);
```

#### FlatMap
Transform each element into zero or more elements:
```java
DataStream<String> flatMapped = stream.flatMap(
    (String line, Collector<String> out) -> {
        for (String word : line.split(" ")) {
            out.collect(word);
        }
    }
);
```

#### KeyBy
Partition stream by key:
```java
KeyedStream<Event, Long> keyed = stream.keyBy(event -> event.getId());
```

#### Reduce
Combine elements with the same key:
```java
DataStream<Event> reduced = keyed.reduce((e1, e2) -> {
    return new Event(e1.getId(), e1.getValue() + e2.getValue());
});
```

### Process Functions
Low-level operations for stateful stream processing:

#### KeyedProcessFunction
Access to keyed state and timers:
```java
public class MyProcessFunction extends KeyedProcessFunction<Key, Input, Output> {
    @Override
    public void processElement(Input value, Context ctx, Collector<Output> out) {
        // Process element
        // Access state: getRuntimeContext().getState(...)
        // Register timers: ctx.timerService().registerEventTimeTimer(...)
    }

    @Override
    public void onTimer(long timestamp, OnTimerContext ctx, Collector<Output> out) {
        // Timer callback
    }
}
```

### State
Flink provides different types of state for stateful stream processing:

#### ValueState
Holds a single value:
```java
ValueStateDescriptor<Integer> descriptor =
    new ValueStateDescriptor<>("count", Integer.class);
ValueState<Integer> state = getRuntimeContext().getState(descriptor);

// Use state
Integer current = state.value();
state.update(current + 1);
```

#### ListState
Holds a list of values:
```java
ListStateDescriptor<Event> descriptor =
    new ListStateDescriptor<>("events", Event.class);
ListState<Event> state = getRuntimeContext().getListState(descriptor);

// Use state
state.add(event);
for (Event e : state.get()) {
    // Process each event
}
```

### Sinks
Where processed data is written:
```java
stream.addSink(new CustomSinkFunction());
stream.writeAsText("output.txt");
```

### Execution
Start the Flink job:
```java
env.execute("Job Name");
```

## Example: Word Count
```java
public class WordCount {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        StreamExecutionEnvironment env =
            StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();

        DataStream<String> text = env.readTextFile("input.txt");

        DataStream<Tuple2<String, Integer>> counts = text
            .flatMap((String line, Collector<Tuple2<String, Integer>> out) -> {
                for (String word : line.split(" ")) {
                    out.collect(new Tuple2<>(word, 1));
                }
            })
            .returns(Types.TUPLE(Types.STRING, Types.INT))
            .keyBy(tuple -> tuple.f0)
            .sum(1);

        counts.print();

        env.execute("Word Count");
    }
}
```

## Reading CSV Files

### Custom Source Function
For reading CSV files (including gzipped):
```java
public class CsvSourceFunction implements SourceFunction<MyType> {
    private String filePath;

    @Override
    public void run(SourceContext<MyType> ctx) throws Exception {
        InputStream inputStream;
        if (filePath.endsWith(".gz")) {
            inputStream = new GZIPInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath));
        } else {
            inputStream = new FileInputStream(filePath);
        }

        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(
            new InputStreamReader(inputStream)
        );

        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            MyType record = parseCSV(line);
            ctx.collect(record);
        }

        reader.close();
    }

    @Override
    public void cancel() {
        // Cleanup
    }
}
```

## Common Patterns

### Filter and Transform
```java
stream
    .filter(event -> event.getType() == EventType.SUBMIT)
    .map(event -> new ProcessedEvent(event));
```

### Group by Key and Aggregate
```java
stream
    .keyBy(event -> event.getJobId())
    .reduce((e1, e2) -> combine(e1, e2));
```

### Write to File Sink
```java
stream.writeAsText("output.txt", WriteMode.OVERWRITE);
```

## Resources
- [Flink Documentation](https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/)
- [DataStream API](https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/dev/datastream/overview/)

